        paragraphs: [
          "From a front-end engineering standpoint, automating **WhatsApp Web** in modern browsers is non-trivial. WhatsApp does not use standard `<textarea>` elements; it uses Meta's **Lexical rich-text editor** framework hosted inside a `div[contenteditable=\"true\"][data-tab=\"10\"]`.",
          "Direct property assignments such as `el.value = text` or `el.textContent = text` fail completely because Lexical maintains an internal virtual state. Any change made without triggering native event flows is wiped out immediately.",
          "During development, we resolved two critical real-world automation challenges:",
          "**• Challenge #1: Avoiding Double Submissions (Idempotency Lock):** Firing an automated submit click alongside a fallback `Enter` event risked dispatching the message twice. We engineered a strict idempotency lock: verifying active DOM text, checking an in-memory `contactedIds` set, and awaiting confirmation that the input box cleared before allowing any retry.",
          "**• Challenge #2: Handling Multiline Text and Newlines:** Using Chrome's `document.execCommand('insertText')` frequently stripped `\\n` line breaks when lines lacked trailing spaces. We replaced this with a synthetic **`ClipboardEvent('paste')`** carrying a `DataTransfer` object with `text/plain`, coupled with a regex sanitizer (`safeText`) and an optional **Review Mode checkbox** to let the human operator inspect the populated message before sending."
        ],
        codeLabel: "Safe Multiline Text Injection into WhatsApp's Lexical Editor (content.js)",
        code: `async function writeIntoLexicalEditor(el, text, clearFirst = true) {
  if (!el) return false;
  realClick(el);
  el.focus();
  await sleep(80);

  // Ensure trailing whitespace before each newline to prevent glued words
  const safeText = text.replace(/\\r\\n/g, "\\n").replace(/([^\\s\\n])\\n/g, "$1 \\n");

  // Dispatch synthetic ClipboardEvent("paste") so Lexical creates clean paragraph nodes
  // without triggering premature submission on multiline templates
  const dt = new DataTransfer();
  dt.setData("text/plain", safeText);
  const pasteEvt = new ClipboardEvent("paste", {
    clipboardData: dt,
    bubbles: true,
    cancelable: true
  });
  el.dispatchEvent(pasteEvt);
  await sleep(150);
  el.dispatchEvent(new InputEvent("input", { bubbles: true }));
  return true;
}`
